{"type":"message_start","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_cObl8bbQBPSVvDzSbpSBFvkF","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Refactoring Applied\n\n**Naming evaluation:** `nextGeneration`, `liveCellKeys`, `neighborCounts`, and `isAliveInNextGeneration` accurately describe their responsibilities. No rename was needed.\n\nChanged `src/game-of-life.ts` to replace a `flatMap` callback that conditionally returned either one cell or an empty array with an explicit:\n\n1. `filter` for cells that survive or are born.\n2. `map` to convert their keys into `Cell` tuples.\n\nThis separates eligibility from coordinate conversion, making the Game of Life rule easier to read.\n\n### APP Mass\n\n**Before**\n- Constants: 4 = 4\n- Bindings: 5 = 5\n- Invocations: 5 = 10\n- Conditionals: 1 = 4\n- Loops: 1 = 5\n- Assignments: 0 = 0\n- **Total: 28**\n\n**After**\n- Constants: 3 = 3\n- Bindings: 5 = 5\n- Invocations: 6 = 12\n- Conditionals: 1 = 4\n- Loops: 2 = 10\n- Assignments: 0 = 0\n- **Total: 34**\n\nThe mass increased by 6 because the transformation is expressed as two explicit collection operations. This is retained because Rule 2 (reveals intent) takes priority over APP mass: filtering eligible cells before mapping their coordinates removes the mixed return shape (`Cell[] | []`) from the callback.\n\n### Test Status\n\nAttempted `pnpm test` both before and after the change. It remains blocked by the environment:\n\n```text\nsh: 1: vitest: not found\n```\n\nTherefore, tests could not be verified as green. The refactor preserves behavior structurally: the same survival/birth predicate is used, and qualifying keys are converted to the same cell tuples."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_07-07-49_game-of-life-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_gpt-5-6-terra/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/game-of-life.spe