ils.\n\n\nCommand exited with code 1"}],"details":{},"isError":true,"timestamp":1784963464427},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_LgEF7B19aOeQxcb8praz0qHI","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"undefined\n ERR_PNPM_RECURSIVE_EXEC_FIRST_FAIL  Command \"tsc\" not found\n\n\nCommand exited with code 254"}],"details":{},"isError":true,"timestamp":1784963464427},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_mZOKj1SzHj4lmhVcASlbWzcb","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export type Cell = [number, number];\n\nconst toCellKey = (x: number, y: number): string => `${x},${y}`;\n\nexport function nextGeneration(liveCells: Cell[]): Cell[] {\n  const liveCellKeys = new Set(liveCells.map(([x, y]) => toCellKey(x, y)));\n  const neighbourCounts = new Map<string, number>();\n\n  for (const [x, y] of liveCells) {\n    for (let deltaX = -1; deltaX <= 1; deltaX += 1) {\n      for (let deltaY = -1; deltaY <= 1; deltaY += 1) {\n        if (deltaX === 0 && deltaY === 0) continue;\n        const neighbouringCellKey = toCellKey(x + deltaX, y + deltaY);\n        neighbourCounts.set(\n          neighbouringCellKey,\n          (neighbourCounts.get(neighbouringCellKey) ?? 0) + 1,\n        );\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  return [...neighbourCounts].flatMap(([key, count]) => {\n    const [x, y] = key.split(\",\").map(Number);\n    return count === 3 || (count === 2 && liveCellKeys.has(key)) ? [[x, y] as Cell] : [];\n  });\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784963464427},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Naming Evaluation**\n- `nextGeneration` accurately describes the function’s current purpose; retained.\n- Renamed local `neighborKey` to `neighbouringCellKey` so it clearly identifies the key as belonging to the adjacent cell being counted.\n\n**Simple Design Evaluation**\n1. **Tests pass:** verification is blocked by the environment: `pnpm test` fails because `vitest` is not installed/executable. `pnpm exec tsc --noEmit` is likewise unavailable.\n2